From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dmayala <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:11:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0054z] drm/a9_eink: 0053 settle and latch outside eng_lock,
 settle clock from the first low reading, per-boot cap

Review 89 (M4). The waveform-end PG sample of patch 0053 is taken under
eng_lock (read and count only); the settle, the latch and the ordered
power-off run after the update's mutex_unlock, as every other rail check
does (fix-0040 / review 22). A latch there counts as an abort and leaves
the full Clear owed. The settle window and the reported duration count from
the first low reading (the 0052 read), not from the settle entry. A 0052 low
already high on the re-read is counted (reread_high). New parameter
pg_settle_total_max (default 30, 0 = never settle) caps recovered dips per
boot. rail_diag's diag_settle line gains total_max, cap_skip, reread_high
and the clock origin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
